    "updated_at": "2026-11-16T19:13:45Z",
    "body": "Thank you again for this report. It is fixed in `main` by PR #2206.\n\nWhen the MCP `post` tool gets a post name, the stored script options now apply if the name is the post of the document. If the name is a different post, the tool gives a warning in the log. It does not drop the options without a word. This also works for one program per operation.\n\nThe fix ships in the next release (v0.23.0). You can test it now with a build from `main`.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
